.Dd August 17, 2026
.Dt WIFI-TUI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wifi-tui
.Nd interactive terminal Wi-Fi controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a full-screen
.Xr ncurses 3
front end for the wireless plumbing in the FreeBSD base system.
It lists nearby access points, associates with open, WPA2-PSK, WPA3-SAE and
WEP networks, handles hidden SSIDs, and shows the current IPv4 address,
netmask, default gateway and DNS servers.
.Pp
.Nm
does not talk to the kernel directly.
It drives the same programs an administrator would use by hand:
.Bl -tag -width "resolv.conf" -offset indent
.It Xr wpa_cli 8
scanning, association and saved network profiles
.It Xr ifconfig 8
wireless interface discovery, IPv4 address and netmask
.It Xr netstat 1
the default gateway for the interface
.It Pa /etc/resolv.conf
the list of DNS servers
.It Xr dhclient 8
DHCP, and only when the interface has no IPv4 address after associating
.El
.Pp
The wireless interface is chosen automatically: the
.Dq wlan
interface group is consulted first, and an interface that is already
associated wins over one that is merely present.
.Ss Keys
.Bl -tag -width "Home / End, PgUp / PgDn" -offset indent
.It Ic Up No / Ic Down
Select a network.
.It Ic Left No / Ic Right
Move the focus between the network list and the status panel.
.It Ic Enter
Connect to the selected network.
.It Ic a
Add or connect to a custom or hidden SSID.
.It Ic r
Rescan for nearby networks.
.It Ic d
Disconnect the wireless interface.
.It Ic Home No / Ic End , Ic PgUp No / Ic PgDn
Move through a long list.
.It Ic q
Quit.
.El
.Ss Connecting
When the selected SSID already has a profile in
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ,
.Nm
activates it and never asks for a passphrase.
Otherwise it prompts, creates a new network with
.Cm add_network ,
and selects it.
Passphrases are handed to
.Xr wpa_cli 8
over standard input rather than on the command line, so they do not appear in
.Xr ps 1
output.
A 64 digit hexadecimal PSK, or a 10 or 26 digit hexadecimal WEP key, is passed
through as a raw key instead of a passphrase.
.Pp
A newly created profile lives only in the running supplicant unless
.Va update_config Ns = Ns Li 1
is set in
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ;
.Nm
reports which of the two happened.
.Pp
Because
.Cm select_network
disables every other profile, a failed association is followed by
.Cm enable_network all
and
.Cm reconnect
so that the machine returns to normal roaming.
.Pp
WPA Enterprise
.Pq 802.1X
networks are not configurable from the interface.
They need an
.Va eap ,
.Va identity
and
.Va password
block in
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ;
once that exists,
.Nm
activates the profile like any other.
.Ss Read-only mode
If the
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
control socket cannot be reached,
.Nm
falls back to listing the
.Xr net80211 4
scan cache through
.Ic ifconfig Ar interface Cm list scan .
The header shows
.Dq ifconfig (read-only)
and connecting and disconnecting are refused.
This is what a missing or unstarted supplicant looks like, not an error in
itself.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Both variables are ignored when the process is running set-user-ID or
set-group-ID, as reported by
.Xr issetugid 2 .
.Bl -tag -width "WIFI_TUI_RESOLV_CONF"
.It Ev WIFI_TUI_RESOLV_CONF
Path to the resolver configuration to read DNS servers from.
Defaults to
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf .
.It Ev WIFI_TUI_WPA_CTRL
Control socket directory passed to
.Xr wpa_cli 8
as
.Fl p .
Defaults to letting
.Xr wpa_cli 8
choose, which is
.Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/wpa_supplicant.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf
supplicant configuration and saved networks
.It Pa /etc/resolv.conf
DNS servers shown in the status panel
.It Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant
control socket directory
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Configure the interface once in
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
replacing
.Li iwlwifi0
with the wireless device from
.Ic sysctl net.wlan.devices :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wlans_iwlwifi0="wlan0"
ifconfig_wlan0="WPA SYNCDHCP"
.Ed
.Pp
Allow the
.Li wheel
group to use the control socket, in
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ctrl_interface=/var/run/wpa_supplicant
ctrl_interface_group=wheel
update_config=1
.Ed
.Pp
Then run
.Nm
as an ordinary user in that group.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr netstat 1 ,
.Xr net80211 4 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ,
.Xr dhclient 8 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr wpa_cli 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An HIRECHE BAGHDAD BELKHEIR
.Sh CAVEATS
Triggering a scan and changing the supplicant's configuration both require
access to the control socket.
Without it
.Nm
starts in read-only mode.
Running the program under
.Xr sudo 8
works but is rarely necessary; adding your account to the group named by
.Va ctrl_interface_group
is the better arrangement.
.Pp
Only IPv4 addressing is displayed.
